-- title:
--   The generating set of `finPts` is already a subgroup
-- statement:
--   Fix natural numbers $N_0$ and $p$ with $N_0 \neq 0$, $p$ prime and nonzero, together with a hypothesis $h_{pN_0}$ that $p \nmid N_0$; let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ satisfying `A.LiesOverPrime p`, i.e. $p$ is a nonunit of $A$, let $\Lambda$ be a `LevelData N₀ p A` (in particular providing a morphism $\sigma_A \colon \operatorname{Spec} A \to$ `base p` with `barPt A` followed by $\sigma_A$ equal to the generic point `genPt p`), and let $O$ be a `JZeroNeronObjectAtP N₀ p hpN₀ A hA Λ`, whose data include a scheme $G$ over `base p` with structure morphism $g$, a relative group law $O.L$ on $g$, and a bijection $O.\mathrm{pts}$ from $\mathrm{JZero}(N_0 p)$, the degree-zero divisor class group $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ of the modular function field at level $N_0p$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, onto the sections of $g$ over `genPt p`. Then for every $m \in \mathbb{N}$ and every $x \in \mathrm{JZero}(N_0 p)$: $x$ lies in $O.\mathrm{finPts}\, m$, which is by definition the subgroup generated by the set of those $y$ with $m \cdot y = 0$ whose point $O.\mathrm{pts}\, y$ satisfies `ExtendsToPlace`, if and only if $x$ itself belongs to that generating set, i.e. $m \cdot x = 0$ and there is a section $s$ of $g$ over $\sigma_A$ with $O.\mathrm{pts}\, x$ equal to `barPt A` followed by $s$.
--
--   This unfolds the definition of the finite (i.e. $A$-integral) part of the $m$-torsion of $J_0(N_0p)$ attached to a Néron object at $p$: the set of $m$-torsion classes whose $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-point on the Néron object extends to an $A$-point is shown to be closed under the group operations, so that taking the generated subgroup changes nothing. It is used in the monodromy and Frobenius computations on the Tate module of $\mathrm{JZero}$ at level divisible by $p$, and in the construction of Néron objects from a level model.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_JZeroNeronObjectAtP_mem_finPts_iff.lean

